+        # Self-tuning image size: whatever GTK actually gives the image region
+        # is what the preview gets decoded at, so the hand-computed 286x148
+        # above is only ever a first guess and cannot rot.
+        #
+        # Two hazards, both paid for elsewhere in this codebase and both real:
+        #   * setting a pixbuf from inside a size-allocate handler re-triggers
+        #     allocation -> loop. Hence the handler is on the CONTAINER, the
+        #     reload is deferred to GLib.idle_add, and a pending reload is
+        #     coalesced with _thumb_reload_pending.
+        #   * KlippyGtk.PixbufFromFile is @lru_cache(maxsize=500) keyed on
+        #     (path, w, h). An unquantised stream of allocations would fill 500
+        #     near-identical ~170KB pixbufs on a 512MB Orange Pi. Quantising to
